      "Mubadala Investment Company (“Mubadala”), an Abu Dhabi sovereign investor, announced the signing of a strategic research partnership with Khalifa University of Science and Technology at the Abu Dhabi Future Health Summit 2026, launching the Life Sciences Innovation Program (LSIP). The program will focus on early-stage research across therapeutics, medical devices and other healthcare technologies. Mubadala Bio, Mubadala’s wholly owned life sciences company, and Khalifa University Enterprises Company, Khalifa University’s business and investment arm, will run LSIP jointly with Khalifa University as the delivery partner. The partnership marks an important step in advancing the UAE’s national life sciences ambitions by bringing academic research and industry expertise together.",
